The product card ships with this CSS:

.card { display: grid; gap: 16px; padding: 16px; }
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .card { grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr; }
}

The same card is placed in the main column (600px wide) and in a 300px-wide sidebar. A customer views the page in a browser window that is 1440px wide. What does the sidebar card do?
